  "headline": [
    "ORT Web CANNOT run in an MV3 service worker: import() is disallowed on ServiceWorkerGlobalScope by the HTML specification. Specification-level, not configuration. Independently validates constitution section 5.",
    "ORT Web DOES work in the chrome.offscreen document AND in a dedicated worker inside it - both backends, headful and headless, output element-exact.",
    "Firefox MV3 event page runs ORT on both backends (Windows) and on WASM (Linux).",
    "ORT Web runs entirely from PACKAGED LOCAL FILES - no network fetch for runtime or model. This answers an open S-02a-2a question: packaged-only origin is feasible.",
    "Linux WebGPU failures are environmental (WSL2 has no /dev/dri, 0 Vulkan ICDs; Firefox Linux has dom.webgpu.enabled off) - the same code succeeds on Windows.",
    "WASM measured faster than WebGPU here. The model is TWO elementwise ops, so GPU transfer cannot amortise. NOT a backend comparison and must not be quoted as one."
  ],
  "not_established": [
    "the twenty model cells - QG-03 stands entirely open",
    "S-04: three concurrent sessions in one WASM heap",
    "any backend ranking or latency budget",
    "threaded WASM (numThreads pinned to 1 throughout)",
    "native Linux with a real GPU"
  ]
